# Ingest API & OpenAPI contract (Hermes)

Third-party agents (Hermes, cron jobs) use **`GET /openapi.json`** or **`GET /openapi.yaml`** as the **source of truth**. The spec is generated at runtime from the same Zod schemas that validate `POST /api/ingest/*` requests. **`GET /developers`** embeds Swagger UI for the same spec.

## When adding or changing an ingest resource

1. **Zod schema** — `modules/ingest/schemas/<resource>.ts` (request body + types).
2. **Route** — `app/api/ingest/<resource>/route.ts` using `handleIngestPost` + schema.
3. **Repository** — `lib/repositories/ingest/<resource>.ts` (admin Supabase writes).
4. **Register OpenAPI** — add path in `modules/ingest/openapi/registry.ts` via `registerIngestPost`.
5. **Route manifest** — append `"/api/ingest/<resource>"` to `INGEST_ROUTE_PATHS` in `modules/ingest/routes.ts`.
6. **Tests** — schema test + route test; `modules/ingest/openapi/__tests__/contract-sync.test.ts` must pass (paths ↔ filesystem ↔ OpenAPI).
7. **Docs** — update bullet list on `app/developers/page.tsx` if user-facing resource list changes; add a row to `modules/ingest/HERMES.md` resource mapping table.

Do **not** hand-edit `openapi.json` as a separate artifact. Do **not** document ingest shapes only in Markdown.

## Auth & env

- Bearer `INGEST_TOKEN` (server-only). Document in `.env.example`.
- Hermes env: `KARRIQI_URL`, `INGEST_TOKEN`, `USER_ID` (maps to body `userId`).

## Future resources

New ingest endpoints follow `POST /api/ingest/<resource>` (e.g. `apartment` when added). Same checklist as above.
